WEBVTT

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.375
We've gained control of the bridge here!

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.085
All platoons, head for the city.

00:00:44.085 --> 00:00:46.713
Guard the bridge exit to
the enemy city with your lives!

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.089
The enemy's taken the bridge.

00:00:48.089 --> 00:00:48.882
Blow it!

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.884
They're coming in!

00:00:53.845 --> 00:00:56.431
Have the 14th and 16th
Platoons lead the landing assault.

00:00:56.431 --> 00:01:00.226
And blow this bridge. Do not
let the enemy reach our soil!

00:01:02.354 --> 00:01:04.689
We split into two groups,
avoid a frontal breakthrough.

00:01:04.689 --> 00:01:06.024
Nina still hasn't arrived.

00:01:06.024 --> 00:01:07.901
Irrelevant. Commencing
the operation takes priority.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.527
Sir!

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:21.039
"Capture the Flag!"

00:01:26.044 --> 00:01:26.711
We can make it.

00:01:26.711 --> 00:01:27.921
Impossible for you, maggot!

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.756
I'll go!

00:01:43.687 --> 00:01:46.064
A little more... Just a little more!

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:52.028
--It's too dangerous!
--What are you doing?!

00:01:52.028 --> 00:01:53.863
It's a trap!

00:01:55.865 --> 00:01:59.035
At that rate, you'd have fallen
ass-backwards down the tower!

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:06.251
Zuellni's flag has been captured!

00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:12.549
Why did you interfere?! We were winning!

00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:15.510
If I hadn't pulled you back
down, you'd be dead by now!

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:18.513
If it will save Zuellni,
I don't care about my life!

00:02:18.722 --> 00:02:21.725
Please move! Please clear a path!

00:02:21.725 --> 00:02:25.854
We had refined tactics and
racked up training for this day,

00:02:25.854 --> 00:02:29.566
and yet those pissant soldiers had...

00:02:53.715 --> 00:02:56.384
<i>We can't lose.</i>

00:02:59.054 --> 00:03:02.932
<i>We have to win or it means nothing!</i>

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:09.022
<i>Brave your truth and brave yourself </i>

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:12.567
<i>So we can go somewhere with the dite</i>

00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:20.283
<i>Keep hope alive, now we</i>
<i>wanna find the new world</i>

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:25.872
<i>Roaming around the city having lost my map</i>

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:29.209
<i>Even a dying world</i>

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:36.049
<i>Let me hear a life deep</i>
<i>within that won't stop running</i>

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:39.010
<i>I seared the undying light into my eyes</i>

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:42.514
<i>Refusing to shut them</i>
<i>even when they dried</i>

00:03:42.514 --> 00:03:49.229
<i>I don't believe anything</i>
<i>I can obtain without getting hurt</i>

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:55.443
<i>A single emotion</i>
<i>directed toward someone</i>

00:03:55.443 --> 00:04:02.701
<i>Splits the steel darkness</i>
<i>like the light of morning</i>

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:07.372
<i>One day brave your</i>
<i>truth and brave yourself</i>

00:04:07.372 --> 00:04:10.875
<i>So you will drastically change</i>

00:04:10.875 --> 00:04:16.715
<i>Compounded strength and prayers</i>

00:04:16.715 --> 00:04:20.427
<i>Intersecting futures</i>
<i>and wishes held close</i>

00:04:20.427 --> 00:04:24.014
<i>I will give these to no one</i>

00:04:24.014 --> 00:04:25.515
<i>Just tough and alive</i>

00:04:25.515 --> 00:04:31.521
<i>It links our hearts</i>

00:04:36.526 --> 00:04:37.777
He's late!

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:40.405
Don't tell me he's made a run for it!

00:04:40.405 --> 00:04:42.949
You dragged him in against his will, right?

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:44.242
That'd make someone want to run.

00:04:44.242 --> 00:04:44.951
What?!

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:46.453
Uh, nothing.

00:04:46.453 --> 00:04:49.414
Um, look, maybe he just got lost.

00:04:49.414 --> 00:04:51.750
I doubt there would be
cause for him to get lost.

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:54.419
You don't have to contradict me, you know.

00:04:54.419 --> 00:04:57.547
It's okay. He'll be here soon.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.467
Sorry, um...

00:05:01.009 --> 00:05:02.344
Let me introduce you to everyone.

00:05:02.344 --> 00:05:05.513
This is our new member, Layfon Alseif.

00:05:05.513 --> 00:05:07.223
Uh, about that...

00:05:07.223 --> 00:05:10.393
That's Sharnid Elipton, fourth
year, our sharpshooter.

00:05:10.393 --> 00:05:11.519
Heya.

00:05:11.519 --> 00:05:14.272
That's Harley Sutton,
third year, our dite mechanic.

00:05:14.272 --> 00:05:15.190
A pleasure.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:16.274
--And finally...
--Um, I...

00:05:16.274 --> 00:05:19.194
Felli Loss, second year, our nen'i operator.

00:05:19.194 --> 00:05:20.779
Uh, the thing is...

00:05:20.779 --> 00:05:26.201
And there's me, Nina Antalk, third-year
Military Arts student, 17th Platoon leader.

00:05:26.868 --> 00:05:30.622
What happened to your 17th
Platoon badge? I gave it to you, yes?

00:05:30.622 --> 00:05:32.874
I can't join the platoon after all.

00:05:33.541 --> 00:05:36.544
My part-time job cleaning at the
machinery department takes up my nights.

00:05:36.544 --> 00:05:39.130
Don't you worry about that!

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:41.007
Restoration.

00:05:41.216 --> 00:05:44.844
I'm going to give you a test now.
There's no need to be nervous.

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:47.097
Harley, get them out.

00:05:47.097 --> 00:05:50.183
We're just going to decide your
position for the next competition.

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:52.018
The next competition?

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:54.562
These are practice dites.

00:05:54.562 --> 00:05:57.774
They haven't been inputted with user
data, so they shouldn't have any special quirks.

00:05:57.774 --> 00:05:59.609
Which one will you use?

00:05:59.609 --> 00:06:01.611
Uh, any one will do...

00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:05.031
Restoration.

00:06:07.909 --> 00:06:10.912
I'm coming after you for real.

00:06:16.251 --> 00:06:19.045
I've never seen someone
fend off Nina's initial attack before.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:34.060
You're pretty good at this.

00:06:34.686 --> 00:06:36.855
I won't hold back either!

00:06:43.528 --> 00:06:46.531
Can you use External Ballistic Kei?

00:06:46.531 --> 00:06:48.408
External Ballistic Kei.

00:06:48.408 --> 00:06:50.035
Yes.

00:06:51.119 --> 00:06:53.538
Defend against this!

00:07:18.021 --> 00:07:19.439
How's Layfon?

00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:22.609
If he rests overnight, it looks like he
can get out of the hospital tomorrow.

00:07:22.609 --> 00:07:24.027
Oh, that's good.

00:07:24.027 --> 00:07:25.904
It's not good at all.

00:07:26.196 --> 00:07:29.199
Was it just a fluke that
he evaded my first attack?

00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:32.285
When we were fighting, I could
definitely feel him responding...

00:07:32.285 --> 00:07:36.373
But what was <i>that</i>? Who would
just take that hit full in the face?!

00:07:36.373 --> 00:07:40.585
Even if he couldn't totally defend
against it, that was <i>way </i>too slow!

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:44.381
Nobody's powerful right off the bat.

00:07:45.965 --> 00:07:48.426
You're right. There's no
point in trying to rush things.

00:07:48.426 --> 00:07:50.261
That's right.

00:08:18.206 --> 00:08:21.376
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:08:21.376 --> 00:08:22.961
Ow...

00:08:23.628 --> 00:08:25.255
It <i>doesn't </i>hurt, does it?

00:08:25.255 --> 00:08:29.718
Not if you can repair yourself using
Internal Augmenting Kei to that extent.

00:08:29.884 --> 00:08:33.847
Hey, I fell! From the bed!
So it hurts, as falling would!

00:08:33.847 --> 00:08:35.682
Is that so?

00:08:56.244 --> 00:08:58.204
Um, Senior Felli?

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:02.876
I know now why my brother
went so far as to deceive you

00:09:02.876 --> 00:09:05.712
to have you transferred to
the Military Arts Department.

00:09:05.712 --> 00:09:08.590
Your brother? "Deceive" me?

00:09:09.799 --> 00:09:13.720
Both the difficulties facing the 17th Platoon
and the skirmish at the entrance ceremony

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:17.515
were schemes devised by my
brother, the student council president,

00:09:17.515 --> 00:09:19.601
to get you into the 17th Platoon.

00:09:20.018 --> 00:09:21.728
I'm sure you find it unbelievable.

00:09:21.728 --> 00:09:24.105
Actually...

00:09:24.105 --> 00:09:28.109
My left arm is slightly longer than my right.

00:09:28.109 --> 00:09:31.029
This military uniform should
have been prepared in a hurry,

00:09:31.029 --> 00:09:34.449
but it's a perfect fit, as if it
were tailor made. That's why, huh?

00:09:34.449 --> 00:09:37.619
So your acting slowly was intentional after all.

00:09:37.619 --> 00:09:39.287
Acting slowly?

00:09:39.287 --> 00:09:42.791
Your inability to evade Nina's
attack earlier was intentional, wasn't it?

00:09:44.209 --> 00:09:48.129
You know what nen'i is of course, don't you?

00:09:48.129 --> 00:09:54.928
Nen'i operators manipulate objects with
unseen hands, extract information from them.

00:09:54.928 --> 00:09:58.390
We see what can't be seen, and
sometimes we can project nen'i outward

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:01.267
to speak with those located elsewhere.

00:10:01.267 --> 00:10:03.395
It can't be mastered through training alone,

00:10:03.395 --> 00:10:07.607
and in a real sense is the ability
of the chosen... isn't that right?

00:10:07.607 --> 00:10:13.613
Even so, it seems my quantity of
nen'i cannot be considered normal.

00:10:17.033 --> 00:10:20.537
My brother sought to use this for Zuellni's sake

00:10:20.537 --> 00:10:24.541
and had me forcibly transferred
to the Military Arts Department.

00:10:26.042 --> 00:10:29.713
I resent my brother.

00:10:29.713 --> 00:10:34.050
He will do anything for victory,
no matter how underhanded.

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:37.721
That's why I think you
are just fine the way you are.

00:10:55.030 --> 00:10:58.199
So this is the heart of Regios...

00:11:07.042 --> 00:11:11.379
Excuse me! This is my first day,
so I'm not sure what I should...

00:11:11.379 --> 00:11:13.381
Ah! I'll be right up.

00:11:16.718 --> 00:11:20.013
I tell you, it's been rough
since our other guy left...

00:11:20.013 --> 00:11:21.890
Ma'am?!

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:25.101
Layfon! You sneaked out of the hospital?!

00:11:25.101 --> 00:11:27.270
No, I'm better already!

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:31.024
Plus it's my first day, so I
couldn't very well be absent.

00:11:31.024 --> 00:11:36.196
You mean you've recovered from all that
damage? What kind of body have you got?!

00:11:42.869 --> 00:11:47.624
Now I get it. This is why she wouldn't let
me quit with a reason like a part-time job...

00:11:47.624 --> 00:11:51.252
What made you work in a place like this?

00:11:51.252 --> 00:11:53.880
It's rough, but the pay is good.

00:11:55.048 --> 00:11:58.551
My parents were against
the idea of Academic City.

00:11:58.551 --> 00:12:04.057
My coming here was half running away from
home... So they don't send any tuition money.

00:12:04.057 --> 00:12:05.934
Why did you come here?

00:12:05.934 --> 00:12:10.939
This was the only school
I passed the scholarship exam for.

00:12:11.439 --> 00:12:13.358
I'm an orphan and I don't have any money.

00:12:13.358 --> 00:12:15.360
Oh. I'm sorry.

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:18.530
Huh? Not at all.

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:19.364
You want some?

00:12:19.364 --> 00:12:21.366
Thank you!

00:12:22.951 --> 00:12:24.077
It's delicious.

00:12:24.077 --> 00:12:28.039
This is the most popular
boxed lunch you can get delivered.

00:12:28.039 --> 00:12:31.459
Speaking of, I have a boxed lunch of my own.

00:12:31.459 --> 00:12:33.294
Would you care for some?

00:12:33.294 --> 00:12:34.587
It sure looks good.

00:12:34.587 --> 00:12:37.090
It was delivered to my room.

00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:38.466
A new product, huh?

00:12:38.466 --> 00:12:39.718
If you'd like some, help yourself.

00:12:39.718 --> 00:12:41.261
I appreciate it.

00:12:41.261 --> 00:12:43.304
Thanks very much for...

00:12:44.055 --> 00:12:48.101
Your lunch is delicious as well.

00:12:54.274 --> 00:12:57.277
This is so good! It's
delicious. It's <i>too </i>delicious!

00:12:57.277 --> 00:12:59.112
Would you like to trade lunches?

00:12:59.112 --> 00:13:02.032
Is that okay? Is it <i>really</i>
okay? It's okay, right?

00:13:02.032 --> 00:13:03.074
Uh, please.

00:13:03.074 --> 00:13:05.035
Thanks. I'm gonna enjoy this!

00:13:09.122 --> 00:13:11.875
I wonder if he'll say it's delicious...

00:13:11.875 --> 00:13:14.878
What's with you, May-cchi? You're being creepy.

00:13:14.878 --> 00:13:17.047
No, nothing at all, nothing at all.

00:13:17.047 --> 00:13:18.882
Yeah, fine.

00:13:19.716 --> 00:13:23.386
That was <i>so </i>delicious!

00:13:24.846 --> 00:13:27.766
Here's my small way of saying "Thanks."

00:13:27.766 --> 00:13:29.601
Thank you.

00:13:34.022 --> 00:13:36.524
It's delicious. Do they sell this too?

00:13:36.524 --> 00:13:38.193
I made it.

00:13:38.193 --> 00:13:42.614
You should make your own drinks.
The drinking water here tastes terrible.

00:13:44.407 --> 00:13:49.287
Made to live inside Regios like this,
we live our entire lives in a single city

00:13:49.287 --> 00:13:52.207
like birds in a cage.

00:13:52.207 --> 00:13:58.213
On the other hand, there are those who
travel on buses that roam between cities.

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:04.094
They see so many different
worlds that other people don't see.

00:14:04.094 --> 00:14:09.766
I was jealous of them.
That's why I decided to come here.

00:14:10.517 --> 00:14:14.896
But my parents really objected...

00:14:14.896 --> 00:14:16.690
That's why you left home?

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:20.110
They found out I'd taken the exam anyway.

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:24.030
The military arts are the
only thing I'm any good at.

00:14:24.614 --> 00:14:27.867
That's why I enrolled in
the Military Arts Department.

00:14:29.953 --> 00:14:32.872
Not that I'd expect you to understand.

00:14:35.208 --> 00:14:37.210
The competition is tomorrow.

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:40.088
Let's finish up work early tonight.

00:14:40.797 --> 00:14:42.048
It's tomorrow?!

00:14:42.048 --> 00:14:44.884
Huh? Didn't I mention that?

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:50.432
We shouldn't have eaten leisurely and
traded life stories <i>today</i>, should we?

00:14:50.432 --> 00:14:53.393
Hey, sometimes you want
to just try and be serious!

00:14:53.393 --> 00:14:56.438
I have to finish quickly... I have to
sleep or the match will be too hard to--!

00:14:56.438 --> 00:15:00.191
Oh, shut up! You got time to talk,
you got time to work, new boy!

00:15:00.191 --> 00:15:01.234
That's just...

00:15:01.234 --> 00:15:02.193
Look, just work!

00:15:02.193 --> 00:15:03.361
I am!

00:15:03.361 --> 00:15:04.904
Work more!

00:15:09.034 --> 00:15:11.202
So... sleepy...

00:15:11.202 --> 00:15:13.246
Good thing you're made of such strong stuff.

00:15:13.246 --> 00:15:17.042
Otherwise, we'd have had
to withdraw from this match.

00:15:20.879 --> 00:15:23.089
I look forward to our match.

00:15:23.548 --> 00:15:27.385
You think we're equals just
because you lead a platoon?

00:15:28.261 --> 00:15:32.390
Let's see how long your
motley crew can stick it out.

00:15:39.856 --> 00:15:43.193
The outcome of this match
will affect our city's position.

00:15:43.193 --> 00:15:45.862
Stay sharp out there.

00:15:48.239 --> 00:15:51.368
I wonder if Lay-ton's all right...

00:15:51.368 --> 00:15:56.039
Sure he is! After all, he ate
May-cchi's handmade boxed lunch!

00:15:56.039 --> 00:15:57.874
Oh, my.

00:15:59.209 --> 00:16:01.419
What is this cold feeling?!

00:16:02.295 --> 00:16:04.464
We will now begin the competition.

00:16:04.464 --> 00:16:07.634
The 17th Platoon will attack
and the 16th Platoon will defend.

00:16:07.634 --> 00:16:10.136
That's the head of the Military
Arts Department, Vanzeh himself.

00:16:10.136 --> 00:16:12.555
Treat this match as if it
were a real intermunicipal battle.

00:16:12.555 --> 00:16:13.264
Sir.

00:16:13.264 --> 00:16:15.684
Both platoons, take your positions!

00:16:15.892 --> 00:16:19.938
The competition between the 16th
and 17th Platoons will now commence.

00:16:20.689 --> 00:16:25.860
Stray bullets and so on may cause injuries,
so audience members, please stay cautious.

00:16:30.073 --> 00:16:33.368
The only way we can win is
to wipe out the enemy platoon

00:16:33.368 --> 00:16:36.204
or take down the flag
planted behind their lines.

00:16:36.204 --> 00:16:38.123
As defense, what
conditions have to be met to win?

00:16:38.123 --> 00:16:43.294
Protect the flag till time runs out,
or knock down the enemy leader.

00:16:43.294 --> 00:16:45.547
Till he can't get up anymore.

00:16:46.464 --> 00:16:50.218
The enemy will be after me.
I'll act as a decoy to lure them in.

00:16:50.218 --> 00:16:51.803
Looks like our leader's feeling aggressive.

00:16:51.803 --> 00:16:53.471
Layfon, you run in front of the enemy line.

00:16:53.471 --> 00:16:54.848
Sharnid, you cover him.

00:16:54.848 --> 00:16:56.224
Roger that.

00:16:56.224 --> 00:16:58.685
Enemy detected. They're approaching.

00:16:59.894 --> 00:17:01.896
Restoration!

00:17:07.277 --> 00:17:08.903
Got you!

00:17:14.784 --> 00:17:16.411
Ma'am!

00:17:16.703 --> 00:17:17.620
Don't worry about me!

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:19.622
Restoration!

00:17:19.956 --> 00:17:22.876
Sharnid, I'm fine, but give Layfon some backup!

00:17:22.876 --> 00:17:25.587
Easier said than done...

00:17:27.255 --> 00:17:30.091
That new student's moves are pretty bad.

00:17:30.091 --> 00:17:32.135
His kei channeling looks bad, too.

00:17:32.135 --> 00:17:34.763
His prowess is guaranteed.

00:17:34.763 --> 00:17:36.890
What are you hiding?

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:40.185
Zuellni only ever gets the fighters
who haven't come into their own yet.

00:17:40.185 --> 00:17:43.396
To him, this may appear
little more than child's play.

00:17:43.396 --> 00:17:46.358
Well, we're giving this
child's play everything we've got.

00:17:46.941 --> 00:17:50.695
All cities have the same desperation to survive.

00:17:51.112 --> 00:17:55.367
That fact doesn't seem to be reaching him...

00:17:55.367 --> 00:17:59.496
It's not just him.
There's your younger sister.

00:18:01.081 --> 00:18:05.293
The two of them have no motivation, and
Sharnid there has no sense of cooperation.

00:18:05.293 --> 00:18:07.462
The whole platoon's nothing but trouble.

00:18:07.462 --> 00:18:11.883
You need to assign Nina Antalk to a
different platoon, let her get brought up right.

00:18:11.883 --> 00:18:17.847
She herself opposed the idea. Also, it
can't be said that failure produces nothing.

00:18:17.847 --> 00:18:22.185
So the whole platoon is to
be sacrificed for a greater gain?

00:18:22.185 --> 00:18:25.563
Whether or not that's the
case will depend on the outcome.

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:29.192
Restoration!

00:18:31.194 --> 00:18:33.947
Sharnid, why aren't you covering Layfon?

00:18:33.947 --> 00:18:37.742
I just couldn't shoot an enemy battling
so spectacularly with one of our own...

00:18:37.742 --> 00:18:41.454
Felli, you're taking too long to find the
enemy's location. Can't you do it faster?

00:18:41.454 --> 00:18:43.289
This is my limit.

00:19:08.857 --> 00:19:11.234
What a terrible shade of kei...

00:19:17.532 --> 00:19:19.117
Layfon!

00:19:27.625 --> 00:19:30.045
Layfon has withdrawn. Damage unknown.

00:19:30.045 --> 00:19:31.629
What?!

00:19:39.471 --> 00:19:41.097
Yes...

00:19:41.431 --> 00:19:43.058
Darn it!

00:19:45.518 --> 00:19:48.688
It's no problem shooting
enemies when they're by themselves...

00:19:55.528 --> 00:19:58.198
<i>It'd be all right if we lost, right?</i>

00:20:13.922 --> 00:20:15.548
Ma'am!

00:20:18.051 --> 00:20:22.430
You haven't changed at all
from two years ago, maggot.

00:20:25.183 --> 00:20:28.937
It can't be! She still had
that much strength left?!

00:20:28.937 --> 00:20:35.026
Now to put my remaining energy
into a single, focused blast... All of it!

00:20:38.697 --> 00:20:42.701
Is that the way a platoon leader fights?!

00:20:47.789 --> 00:20:49.416
Ma'am!

00:20:54.129 --> 00:20:56.881
Start the countdown.
Sound the siren at 30 seconds.

00:20:56.881 --> 00:20:59.134
I think you've judged a little quickly...

00:20:59.134 --> 00:21:02.387
At this rate, the 17th
Platoon will become useless.

00:21:02.595 --> 00:21:05.515
Fight alone and die alone, huh?!

00:21:05.515 --> 00:21:08.101
Don't go thinking that's the right way!

00:21:08.101 --> 00:21:10.603
<i>Dammit! I can't lose...</i>

00:21:10.603 --> 00:21:12.605
<i>I mustn't lose!</i>

00:21:14.941 --> 00:21:18.611
I can't lose... I mustn't lose!

00:21:18.611 --> 00:21:20.697
<i>She's going to be beaten!</i>

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:32.709
External Ballistic Kei!

00:21:33.877 --> 00:21:36.046
Dragon-Spiral Kei!

00:21:41.634 --> 00:21:45.263
Internal Augmenting Kei, Spiral Kei!

00:21:48.099 --> 00:21:49.726
You...

00:21:50.352 --> 00:21:52.020
The hell?

00:22:13.291 --> 00:22:16.294
--Yes!
--We did it!

00:22:32.769 --> 00:22:35.188
Layfon, that was incredible!

00:22:35.188 --> 00:22:39.859
More to the point, sorry...
This dite can't be used anymore.

00:22:39.859 --> 00:22:45.031
I've never seen that before!
Your kei was too strong for the dite to contain.

00:22:45.031 --> 00:22:48.368
We're going to have to think of
different dite settings for you, huh?

00:22:48.368 --> 00:22:53.748
Dude! Where were you hiding
those claws of yours? Strokey strokey...

00:22:59.212 --> 00:23:00.880
Ma'am!

00:23:23.361 --> 00:23:24.946
Traitor.

00:24:05.236 --> 00:24:08.031
<i>Beyond memory</i>

00:24:08.031 --> 00:24:16.414
<i>A map of the ideal future</i>
<i>you'd been searching for</i>

00:24:16.414 --> 00:24:27.467
<i>Scared of something, not</i>
<i>understanding, trembling alone</i>

00:24:27.467 --> 00:24:38.770
<i>Unable to see you, I'm</i>
<i>always wearing a fake smile</i>

00:24:38.770 --> 00:24:48.029
<i>I was held in your arms</i>

00:24:48.029 --> 00:24:53.618
<i>Fall in love like</i>
<i>you're waking up</i>

00:24:53.618 --> 00:24:59.040
<i>And then take</i>
<i>me into dreamland</i>

00:24:59.040 --> 00:25:04.754
<i>You always, you always</i>

00:25:04.754 --> 00:25:13.555
<i>You always told me tender lies</i>

00:25:23.690 --> 00:25:28.778
<i>Nina makes plain her anger at Layfon having</i>
<i>hidden his extraordinary strength. </i>

00:25:28.778 --> 00:25:32.532
<i>In the midst of this, Nina goes missing while in</i>
<i>pursuit of an enemy in the machinery department</i>

00:25:32.532 --> 00:25:34.367
<i>because Zuellni has suddenly come to a halt.</i>

00:25:34.367 --> 00:25:36.369
<i>Next time, "Electronic Spirit Zuellni" and...</i>

00:25:36.369 --> 00:25:38.048
<i>Restoration!</i>
